Binary incorrect feedback rejects only the submitted output; it does not localize errors or validate a nearby alternative. Before another action, rebuild the evidence from all demonstrations, including no-op and visually heterogeneous pairs. Record role colors, exact changed and preserved cells, candidate rule, and whether the rule reproduces every demo. Identify the specific model correction being tested and the evidence for it.

A demo request and wrong submission each cost one point, so use a request when it can distinguish materially different hypotheses. Tie each request to a named unresolved distinction. If there is no evidence-based candidate that replays every example, prefer targeted information gathering over cycling through speculative variants. Keep the strict action protocol intact; do not add explanatory text to puzzle turns.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792545261/attempts/dc2dcdf57b4240ea8dfdb9832237f673/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-puzzle-solving/references/post-rejection-audit.md"}

